User programs: gcc-14 -static -O2 -Wall -Wextra -Werror
ntsync additionally uses -isystem /work/headers (the frozen installed headers).
Kernel module: original Kbuild, ARCH=arm64 CC=gcc-14 HOSTCC=gcc-14,
M=/work/probe/driver -j2 modules; original source/pristine trees mounted read-only.
Only this test module is signed with the existing kernel's build key.
An initial init-wrapper build failed -Werror=return-type after main was renamed;
declaring its existing nonreturning poweroff helper noreturn corrected the harness.
The final module build had subsecond shared-filesystem clock-skew warnings, no
compiler errors. Actual signed-module loading, API checks and unloading passed.

Payload builder: original usr/gen_init_cpio -t 0; retained tools/k1/selftest-init.c
and tools/k1/boot.sh, no new runner. The small init overlay loads the original
signed ntsync module. The original runtime disk is only a QEMU snapshot scratch
device; no full clone, payload replacement or persistent disk write is made.
K1_ALLOW_QEMU_DRIFT=1 K1_KUNIT_AUTORUN=0 K1_CONSOLE_LOGLEVEL=1 K1_BOOT_TIMEOUT=90
Default hvf-host lane; each diagnostic has a 15-second watchdog.

